      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are adding this at the top of the file\n```\n#if defined(OS_GENERIC)\nstatic const char* INTEROP_FILE_PATH \u003d \"interop_database.conf\";\n#else   // !defined(OS_GENERIC)\nstatic const char* INTEROP_DYNAMIC_FILE_PATH \u003d\n    \"/data/misc/bluedroid/interop_database_dynamic.conf\";\nstatic const char* INTEROP_STATIC_FILE_PATH \u003d\n    \"/apex/com.android.btservices/etc/bluetooth/interop_database.conf\";\n#endif  // defined(OS_GENERIC)\n```\n\n\nThe consequence is that:\n* OS_GENERIC has  `INTEROP_FILE_PATH`\n* !OS_GENERIC has `INTEROP_DYNAMIC_FILE_PATH` and `INTEROP_STATIC_FILE_PATH`\n\nYou need to reflect this when using the variable.\n\nI think what you want is to :\n* Rename INTEROP_FILE_PATH to be INTEROP_STATIC_FILE_PATH\n* add a `if not defined OS_GENERIC` around everything related to dynamic config as you are not managing this option in os_generic\n\n\nThen you should try it by running the test on a host target like this:\n```\natest --host net_test_device\n```\n\nI tried it and I noticed you need a small change in the bp to test it this way (aosp/2380866 - merged today)",
